The bug is in the `push` method. When the buffer is full, the code calculates `self.start + 1` to rotate the window, but it does not wrap `self.start` back to `0` if it exceeds the list length. This causes an `IndexError` when `self.start` reaches the length of the list.

Here is the corrected file:

