class RingBuffer:
    """Fixed-capacity buffer keeping the most recent items; items() returns them oldest first."""

    def __init__(self, capacity):
        if capacity <= 0:
            raise ValueError('capacity must be positive')
        self.capacity, self.data, self.start = capacity, [], 0

    def push(self, x):
        if len(self.data) < self.capacity:
            self.data.append(x)
        else:
            self.data[self.start] = x
            self.start = (self.start + 1) % len(self.data)

    def items(self):
        return self.data[self.start:] + self.data[:self.start]
```

The bug is in the `get` method. It does not move the accessed key to the end of the `OrderedDict`, which means `get()` does not count as a "use" (refresh) of the cache entry. This causes the LRU eviction logic to fail when the accessed item is later evicted.

Here is the corrected file:

